  NOTE on the percentile rules. Their onset fraction is fixed by construction, so b1 - 1 is ~0 (XJTU-SY: -0.003 to -0.001). Their rank correlation is
  not: the floor in floor(n(1-p)) makes u = (i*+1)/n FALL toward 1-p as n grows (here rho(u, n) from -0.82 to -0.56),
  while i*/n RISES toward 1-p (rho(i*/n, n) about +0.86 for pct05). A rank statistic follows a discretisation
  artefact of a few thousandths of life in either direction; the slope does not. This is why b1 - 1 is the
  main statistic of the revision (analysis plan, Section 6).

